/-!
# Parabolic cohomology rank of Γ(N), denominator-free form

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.six_mul_level_mul_finrank_parabolicHoms_Gamma_add_eq`
(`519171ea-ebbc-5f2e-b68a-09223cae681b`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `a35ca822-2aca-5b04-9567-245ee17b3b6d`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a natural number with $2 \le N$, let $\Gamma(N) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ be the
principal congruence subgroup of level $N$, and let $\mu_N$ denote the index in
$\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup $\Gamma(N) \sqcup \langle -1 \rangle$ generated by
$\Gamma(N)$ together with $-1$. Let $\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathrm{par}}(\Gamma(N), \mathbb{Z})$ be the
$\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the additive group of homomorphisms from the additivisation of $\Gamma(N)$
to $\mathbb{Z}$ consisting of those $\varphi$ that vanish on every $\gamma \in \Gamma(N)$ whose
matrix trace satisfies $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma)^2 = 4$, i.e. on all elements of trace $\pm 2$; this is
the group-theoretic parabolic cohomology of $\Gamma(N)$ with $\mathbb{Z}$-coefficients. The
assertion is the identity of natural numbers
$$6N \cdot \mathrm{rank}_{\mathbb{Z}} \, \mathrm{Hom}_{\mathrm{par}}(\Gamma(N), \mathbb{Z}) + 6\mu_N
= 12N + N\mu_N,$$
where the rank is the $\mathbb{Z}$-module rank (`Module.finrank`). Written with denominators, this
says that the rank equals $2\bigl(1 + \mu_N (N-6)/(12N)\bigr)$, twice the genus of $X(N)$; the form
above avoids division and subtraction.

This is the group-cohomological half of the classical computation $\mathrm{rank}\,
H^1_{\mathrm{par}}(\Gamma(N), \mathbb{Z}) = 2\,g(X(N))$, obtained from the freeness of the image of
$\Gamma(N)$ in $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ (no nontrivial torsion for $N \ge 2$) together with the
count of cusps, i.e. of orbits of $\langle T \rangle$ on $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\Gamma(N)$. It
is used to bound the rank of parabolic cohomology of $\Gamma(N)$ by twice the dimension of the space
of cusp forms of weight $2$.

